.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd October 10, 2026
.Dt SYSCTLCMPCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm sysctlcmpctl
.Nd command-line client for the system.Sysctl capability
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm get Ar name
.Nm
.Cm set Ar name Ar value
.Nm
.Cm fmt Ar name
.Nm
.Cm descr Ar name
.Nm
.Cm list Op Ar start-name
.Nm
.Cm interfaces
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads and writes kernel
.Xr sysctl 3
variables through the
.Dq system.Sysctl
capability provided by
.Xr bsdsysctl 8 ,
subject to the caller's per-label policy.
.Cm get
prints the value of
.Ar name ;
.Cm set
assigns the string
.Ar value
to
.Ar name .
.Cm fmt
prints the type/format string of
.Ar name ,
and
.Cm descr
prints its description.
.Cm list
enumerates variable names in order, beginning at
.Ar start-name
or, when it is omitted, at the root.
Every subcommand is subject to the caller's per-label read or write policy.
.Sh INTERFACE INVENTORY
.Cm interfaces
prints one bounded snapshot as index, name, flags, MTU, and link-state fields.
Control bytes, whitespace, and backslashes in names are escaped as hexadecimal
bytes so each interface occupies one output line.
The link state is unknown, down, or up; it is not a connectivity probe.
The caller requires read permission for
.Dq net.routetable
in the provider policy.
The command grants no additional access and performs no writes.
See
.Xr sysctlcmp_interfaces 3
for snapshot size limits and error handling.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sysctl 8 ,
.Xr libsysctlcmp 3 ,
.Xr bsdsysctl 8
